{"title":"tree, butterfly, lightening, tree","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/tree-butterfly-lightening-tree","date":1744966980000,"content":" \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/74282ed7-533a-4283-be69-b0643a078bcb/sketchbook+imags1.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/tag/sketchbook\" target=\"_blank\">life from my sketchbook</a><br /><em>a case study in tiny containers &amp; micro-practices</em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>this page is the result of an exercise I gave myself. I asked myself: </p><ul><li><p>what’s the smallest creative container I can fill — that meets no resistance from my mind?</p></li><li><p>what’s the simplest, most basic medium I can use?  </p></li><li><p>what’s the most low-pressure way to do this? <br /></p></li></ul><p>that week, I drew four squares, and I gave myself the exercise of filling one square a day with whatever I wanted, in <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/micro-practices-as-portals-to-your-art\" target=\"_blank\">micro-practice increments</a> of 3-7-12 minutes each. every morning, I’d sense into what was present in my psyche (mostly trees, it seems), and do a tiny 7 minute sketch. </p><p>then I’d complete the rest of the drawing throughout the day, dipping in and out in the tiny moments between client projects and course work. I noticed that after I created the form and shapes, it was almost as if my hands moved themselves to finish the piece. I felt deep satisfaction of completing one square a day, and wondering what tomorrow’s square would bring.  </p><p>this is my personal creative case study in </p><ul><li><p>the power of tiny circles (a 2.5 x 2.5” square box)</p></li><li><p>completion as providing momentum and fuel</p></li><li><p>layered accumulation over time (daily satisfaction)</p></li><li><p>micro-practice as portals into making my art feel accessible </p></li></ul>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0fc929da-0a0e-4cb2-aad5-11fc14b09fa6/fingers.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n <hr />\n\n\n  <p>where did this come from? after many years of working mostly digital-only in Procreate, I felt the urge to center my work in the physical world. and, as much as I love watercolor and gouache and the density of working with color, it was causing me bottleneck friction to get out the paints and wash the paintbrushes, and wait for layers to dry…</p><p>so I gave myself the limitation of working only with pencil — like I was back in middle school drawing classes again. and maybe pen. I had no intention other than to draw whatever was in my mind. and mostly my mind was full of trees (from walking my dog every morning) and fluttering images of spring. </p><p>that Friday, my week 2 of teaching <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/creative-systems\">creative systems</a>, there was a sudden flash of lightening outside my window. I drew that as my last square.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/b57cecbe-bf44-4f3c-a2de-e99f1340a074/single.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\